//ERR 16 3 16 6
//MSG="This function does not return a value in all control paths"

// `f` returns i32 — deduced from `ret 1` — but only when the `if` is taken.
// Called with -5 it would run off the end of the body, and codegen would emit a
// C function with no `return` on that path, leaving the caller to read whatever
// happened to be in the return register.
//
// This is the base case of the returns-on-all-paths check: an `if` with no
// `else`. 26_if_else_returns_on_both_branches.cpl is the accepted form.
//
// The span is the signature — the name through the last argument — rather than
// the point where control leaves the body, because there is no such point to
// name: the defect is the absence of a statement, so the diagnostic points at
// the function that is missing it. Every case in 73e-80e is reported this way.

fn f n
    if n > 0
        ret 1

fn main
    out "{f(-5)}"
